            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 12</span><h1>Database per Service Pattern</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>25 min</span><span class="lesson-level advanced">Advanced</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Why Database per Service?</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Loose coupling - services can evolve independently</li>
                        <li>Right tool for the job - SQL, NoSQL, Graph per service</li>
                        <li>Independent scaling</li>
                        <li>Failure isolation</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Data Ownership</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-text">Order Service        Inventory Service      Customer Service
┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐       ┌──────────────┐
│   Orders     │    │   Products   │       │  Customers   │
│   OrderItems │    │    Stock     │       │  Addresses   │
└──────┬───────┘    └──────┬───────┘       └──────┬───────┘
       │                   │                      │
       ▼                   ▼                      ▼
  ┌─────────┐         ┌─────────┐           ┌─────────┐
  │ SQL DB  │         │ Redis   │           │ SQL DB  │
  └─────────┘         └─────────┘           └─────────┘</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Cross-Service Queries</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// ❌ NO: Direct database access
var customer = _otherServiceDbContext.Customers.Find(id);

// ✅ YES: API call
var customer = await _customerClient.GetCustomerAsync(id);

// ✅ YES: Keep local cache (eventual consistency)
var customer = await _localCache.GetOrAddAsync(
    $"customer:{id}",
    () =&gt; _customerClient.GetCustomerAsync(id));</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Data Synchronization</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Subscribe to events to keep local copies
public class CustomerUpdatedConsumer : IConsumer&lt;CustomerUpdated&gt;
{
    public async Task Consume(ConsumeContext&lt;CustomerUpdated&gt; context)
    {
        var msg = context.Message;
        
        // Update local read-only copy
        await _localCustomerCache.UpdateAsync(new CustomerInfo
        {
            Id = msg.CustomerId,
            Name = msg.Name,
            Email = msg.Email
        });
    }
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <LessonTakeaways>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Each service owns its data exclusively.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>No direct database sharing between services.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Use events to sync data across services.</LessonTakeaway>
                </LessonTakeaways>
            </div>
